1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:07,427
Today is September 19, 2026.

3
00:00:07,427 --> 00:00:16,103
Overnight, the S&P five hundred and Nasdaq traded in a tight range as weak US manufacturing data offset Fed tightening concerns.

4
00:00:16,103 --> 00:00:20,650
Treasury ten-year yields held near the upper bound of their recent band.

5
00:00:20,650 --> 00:00:26,569
The Fed rate path remains the single dominant variable pricing every asset in the complex.

6
00:00:26,569 --> 00:00:28,922
The core tension is this.

7
00:00:28,922 --> 00:00:31,312
Manufacturing is cooling.

8
00:00:31,312 --> 00:00:34,302
That weakens the case for further hikes.

9
00:00:34,302 --> 00:00:36,741
But inflation is not dead.

10
00:00:36,741 --> 00:00:38,898
The Fed is boxed in.

11
00:00:38,898 --> 00:00:44,768
Meanwhile, the Bank of Japan hiked twenty-five basis points to one and a quarter percent.

12
00:00:44,768 --> 00:00:47,378
Two dissenting votes on the board.

13
00:00:47,378 --> 00:00:50,834
The shortest gap between hikes in thirty years.

14
00:00:50,834 --> 00:00:53,983
The market's immediate verdict was underwhelming.

15
00:00:53,983 --> 00:00:56,814
Then Tokyo intervened in the yen.

16
00:00:56,814 --> 00:00:59,804
The carry trade supercycle is turning.

17
00:00:59,804 --> 00:01:01,826
Think about the scale.

18
00:01:01,826 --> 00:01:07,023
Japanese investors hold roughly five trillion dollars in overseas assets.

19
00:01:07,023 --> 00:01:11,300
Two and a half trillion sits in US equities and Treasuries.

20
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:16,557
As domestic yields rise, that capital has a gravitational pull back home.

21
00:01:16,557 --> 00:01:20,160
Global liquidity is being restructured in real time.

22
00:01:20,160 --> 00:01:22,304
This is not a headline.

23
00:01:22,304 --> 00:01:26,214
This is a structural repricing of the global risk premium.

24
00:01:26,214 --> 00:01:31,630
In a twenty-four hour window, three major central banks made three different calls.

25
00:01:31,630 --> 00:01:33,420
The Fed hiked.

26
00:01:33,420 --> 00:01:35,344
Japan followed.

27
00:01:35,344 --> 00:01:41,091
The Bank of England held at six to three, with three votes wanting a move to four percent.

28
00:01:41,091 --> 00:01:43,640
The pound weakened on the decision.

29
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:46,949
The ECB is signaling more hikes ahead.

30
00:01:46,949 --> 00:01:49,474
Energy costs are the driver.

31
00:01:49,474 --> 00:01:53,248
Diesel in Europe is above three hundred dollars per barrel.

32
00:01:53,248 --> 00:01:56,692
France is weighing strategic reserve releases.

33
00:01:56,692 --> 00:01:59,400
The direction is the same everywhere.

34
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:01,888
Funding costs are rising.

35
00:02:01,888 --> 00:02:04,486
The pace is the only variable.

36
00:02:04,486 --> 00:02:09,633
On the energy front, US diesel hit six dollars and forty cents a gallon.

37
00:02:09,633 --> 00:02:15,099
The administration is weighing export restrictions tied to domestic inventory thresholds.

38
00:02:15,099 --> 00:02:18,701
Short term, that suppresses local prices.

39
00:02:18,701 --> 00:02:23,089
But it forces overseas buyers into the remaining global supply.

40
00:02:23,089 --> 00:02:26,030
International diesel prices spike.

41
00:02:26,030 --> 00:02:29,143
That feeds back into US inflation.

42
00:02:29,143 --> 00:02:31,557
And refiners cut throughput.

43
00:02:31,557 --> 00:02:33,812
Supply tightens again.

44
00:02:33,812 --> 00:02:37,733
It is a policy that solves one problem and creates three.

45
00:02:37,733 --> 00:02:41,728
Now let us connect this to where the capital is actually flowing.

46
00:02:41,728 --> 00:02:45,442
Global equity funds are still seeing net inflows.

47
00:02:45,442 --> 00:02:48,015
But the destination has shifted.

48
00:02:48,015 --> 00:02:51,496
Non-US markets are absorbing more of that money.

49
00:02:51,496 --> 00:02:55,822
US equity funds registered a modest net outflow overnight.

50
00:02:55,822 --> 00:02:57,868
This is not a flight.

51
00:02:57,868 --> 00:03:00,050
It is a reallocation.

52
00:03:00,050 --> 00:03:03,873
Pension funds and insurers are still buying bonds.

53
00:03:03,873 --> 00:03:08,505
Corporate buybacks remain at one point three trillion dollars globally.

54
00:03:08,505 --> 00:03:11,373
The water is moving, not draining.

55
00:03:11,373 --> 00:03:16,079
The AI capital expenditure cycle is the engine under all of this.

56
00:03:16,079 --> 00:03:21,189
Goldman Sachs projects a four hundred and twenty billion dollar collective debt raise.

57
00:03:21,189 --> 00:03:26,569
Amazon, Google, Meta, Microsoft, and Oracle are all in scope.

58
00:03:26,569 --> 00:03:29,755
The timeline runs through 2027.

59
00:03:29,755 --> 00:03:32,942
That is a massive bond supply overhang.

60
00:03:32,942 --> 00:03:35,920
It compresses equity valuations.

61
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:40,368
It raises the cost of capital for every growth story in the index.

62
00:03:40,368 --> 00:03:44,535
The capex cycle runs at least through the end of 2027.

63
00:03:44,535 --> 00:03:48,420
That is a multi-year structural headwind for tech multiples.

64
00:03:48,420 --> 00:03:51,888
On the regulatory front, the pressure is building.

65
00:03:51,888 --> 00:03:58,469
California's governor signed an executive order mandating kill-switch mechanisms for high-risk AI models.

66
00:03:58,469 --> 00:04:03,407
OpenAI and Nvidia leadership are attending the state dinner with the President.

67
00:04:03,407 --> 00:04:07,464
Chip export controls and AI safety are on the table.

68
00:04:07,464 --> 00:04:10,123
Compliance costs are rising.

69
00:04:10,123 --> 00:04:14,045
This is a long-term drag on the sector's margin profile.

70
00:04:14,045 --> 00:04:20,282
And on the innovation side, Anthropic has stood up a physical biology lab in San Francisco.

71
00:04:20,282 --> 00:04:24,302
They are moving from simulation to wet-lab experimentation.

72
00:04:24,302 --> 00:04:27,243
AI-directed robotic biology.

73
00:04:27,243 --> 00:04:30,699
Drug discovery in neglected disease areas.

74
00:04:30,699 --> 00:04:36,005
Meanwhile, their own researchers are sounding alarms about biosecurity risk.

75
00:04:36,005 --> 00:04:39,841
The industry is accelerating and warning at the same time.

76
00:04:39,944 --> 00:04:45,825
The bull case for the AI complex is that this September pullback is a crowded-trade unwind.

77
00:04:45,775 --> 00:04:48,630
CTA funds are still selling.

78
00:04:48,630 --> 00:04:51,241
September is seasonally weak.

79
00:04:51,241 --> 00:04:54,611
October brings the Q3 earnings window.

80
00:04:54,611 --> 00:04:57,221
That is the verification event.

81
00:04:57,221 --> 00:05:02,380
The bear case is that the debt overhang and regulatory costs are not fully priced.

82
00:05:02,380 --> 00:05:06,216
The carry trade reversal adds a second layer of pressure.

83
00:05:06,216 --> 00:05:08,875
Both camps agree on one thing.

84
00:05:08,875 --> 00:05:12,760
The Q3 report card in October is the inflection.

85
00:05:12,760 --> 00:05:16,167
Now, the three names that matter most today.

86
00:05:16,167 --> 00:05:17,772
Nvidia.

87
00:05:17,772 --> 00:05:20,885
The stock is caught between two forces.

88
00:05:20,885 --> 00:05:26,596
On one side, the capex supercycle keeps the data center revenue pipeline loaded.

89
00:05:26,596 --> 00:05:29,856
That runs through 2027 at minimum.

90
00:05:29,856 --> 00:05:34,353
On the other, chip export policy is now a state-dinner topic.

91
00:05:34,353 --> 00:05:38,397
California's kill-switch mandate adds compliance friction.

92
00:05:38,397 --> 00:05:41,265
Institutional positioning is heavy.

93
00:05:41,265 --> 00:05:45,518
The key technical level to watch is the fifty-day moving average.

94
00:05:45,518 --> 00:05:49,464
A close below that on volume signals the next leg down.

95
00:05:49,464 --> 00:05:54,819
A reclaim on the October earnings preview would confirm the dip was a buying opportunity.

96
00:05:54,819 --> 00:06:03,385
Risk management: if the stock loses the round-number support at the prior consolidation shelf, the CTA sell program accelerates.

97
00:06:03,385 --> 00:06:05,665
Do not catch that knife.

98
00:06:05,665 --> 00:06:07,356
Coinbase.

99
00:06:07,356 --> 00:06:10,873
Bitcoin touched eighty thousand dollars overnight.

100
00:06:10,873 --> 00:06:16,020
The catalyst is the SEC's approval of a tokenized equity trading exemption.

101
00:06:16,020 --> 00:06:21,326
This is the first meaningful step toward on-chain securities compliance in the US.

102
00:06:21,326 --> 00:06:26,449
Institutional research is drawing the parallel to gold as a debt-inflation hedge.

103
00:06:26,449 --> 00:06:30,885
Coinbase benefits directly as the primary regulated exchange.

104
00:06:30,885 --> 00:06:34,390
The stock is highly beta to the crypto narrative.

105
00:06:34,390 --> 00:06:37,429
Watch the eighty-dollar level on the equity.

106
00:06:37,429 --> 00:06:41,780
A break above on volume confirms institutional accumulation.

107
00:06:41,780 --> 00:06:45,150
A rejection there means the move was speculative.

108
00:06:45,150 --> 00:06:49,831
The SEC approval is a structural catalyst, not a one-day pop.

109
00:06:49,831 --> 00:06:54,084
But the stock needs to hold above the twenty-day average to validate.

110
00:06:54,084 --> 00:06:56,020
Berkshire Hathaway.

111
00:06:56,020 --> 00:07:02,049
Warren Buffett, ninety-six, has officially stepped down as chairman after fifty-six years.

112
00:07:02,049 --> 00:07:04,880
Howard Buffett takes the chairman seat.

113
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:08,128
Greg Abel runs day-to-day operations.

114
00:07:08,128 --> 00:07:11,706
Warren retains a board seat and honorary title.

115
00:07:11,706 --> 00:07:15,003
The market is now pricing the post-Buffett era.

116
00:07:15,003 --> 00:07:17,785
The question is asset stability.

117
00:07:17,785 --> 00:07:21,522
Will the balance sheet be deployed aggressively or preserved?

118
00:07:21,522 --> 00:07:24,598
Watch the first quarterly letter under Abel.

119
00:07:24,598 --> 00:07:28,336
That document will define the new operating philosophy.

120
00:07:28,336 --> 00:07:31,535
For now, the stock is a sentiment trade.

121
00:07:31,535 --> 00:07:33,581
The moat is intact.

122
00:07:33,581 --> 00:07:35,861
The question is the driver.

123
00:07:35,861 --> 00:07:38,520
One final note on positioning.

124
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:43,606
The September options expiry and the buyback quiet period are still active.

125
00:07:43,606 --> 00:07:47,209
That is mechanical downside pressure into month-end.

126
00:07:47,209 --> 00:07:50,689
CTA quant models still have room to sell.

127
00:07:50,689 --> 00:07:53,581
The genuine turning point is October.

128
00:07:53,581 --> 00:07:56,829
Until then, the market is in a range.

129
00:07:56,829 --> 00:07:58,704
Trade the edges.

130
00:07:58,704 --> 00:08:00,738
Respect the levels.

131
00:08:00,738 --> 00:08:03,263
And let the earnings do the talking.

132
00:08:03,263 --> 00:08:07,270
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

133
00:08:07,270 --> 00:08:11,437
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
